"""
Tutorial 9a — survey the flight envelope.

Trims and linearizes the aircraft at 100 × 100 flight conditions. `Envelope` shows how the
trimmed angle of attack, thrust, elevator and pitch divergence rate change with airspeed
and altitude, and where the bank's nodes sit: one scheduling variable is not enough across
this range.
"""
analysis TutorialEnvelope
  extends F16ModelWorkshop.EnvelopeAnalysis(velocities = [140.0, 250.0], altitudes = [0.0, 9000.0], points = 100)
  model = F16ModelWorkshop.Plant.F16PlantModel()
end

"""
Tutorial 9b — fly the envelope-scheduled MPC.

`FlightResponse` shows both references tracked, and the airspeed and altitude weights with
which the bank blends its nine members.
"""
analysis TutorialEnvelopeMPC
  extends F16ModelWorkshop.FlightAnalysis(stop = 80.0, panels = ["Airspeed (m/s): f16plant.vt, vt_reference", "Altitude (m): f16plant.alt, alt_reference", "Airspeed weights of the bank (140, 175, 210 m/s): sched_vt.w[1], sched_vt.w[2], sched_vt.w[3]", "Altitude weights of the bank (1000, 4000, 7000 m): sched_alt.w[1], sched_alt.w[2], sched_alt.w[3]", "Elevator (deg): f16plant.el", "Thrust (N): f16plant.T"])
  model = EnvelopeMPCDemo()
end

"""
Tutorial 9c — rebuild the bank's trim table.

Re-trims the aircraft at the nodes of `assets/envelope_trim_alpha.csv` and rewrites it. To
move the grid, edit the table's first column (airspeeds) or header row (altitudes), then
run this.
"""
analysis TutorialEnvelopeTable
  extends F16ModelWorkshop.EnvelopeAnalysis(velocities = [140.0, 250.0], altitudes = [0.0, 9000.0], points = 2, table_dir = "assets")
  model = F16ModelWorkshop.Plant.F16PlantModel()
end
